WyvernCorpseHead: {
	DisplayName: The Great Wyvern's Corpse
	BossBarDisplayName: THE GREAT WYVERN'S CORPSE
	InternalName: WyvernCorpse
	DespawnMessage: The Wyvern escapes to look for more food...
	BestiaryEntry1:
		'''
		A once magnificent wonder of the open skies. It was the paragon of truth, innocence, and sanity up until the moment it fell from the sky.
		The Great Wyvern had amassed a devout following among many societies, as its generosity and wisdom were near unmatched.
		And so, to dare harm, let alone slay, such a divine figure is unforgivable. A crime without equal and beyond compare, even to genocide.
		Despite that, someone actually took it upon themselves to shoot The Great Wyvern as it flew over, sending it careening into the Crimson.
		'''
	Hint: Not much remains of the Great Wyvern, but if you can repurpose the small amounts of its soul inside the [i:DestroyerTest/Item_BlessingAltar] Blessing Altar, you may be able to draw it to you.
	BestiaryEntry2:
		'''
		The crimson hivemind, whos members were too feeble-minded to understand divinity, wasted no time gorging on the Wyvern's Bountiful feathers and fur.
		The flesh though, they could not eat. Sinking their teeth and mandibles into it would take the same amount of effort as trying to compress a star into the size of a grain of salt.
		So now, only the flesh and bones remain, only consumable by the Crimson itself, and anyone of divine stature themselves.
		The meat has hardened into crimstone, and the bones have dried and hardened stronger than lizard bricks.
		'''
	Bestiary: Mods.DestroyerTest.NPCs.WyvernCorpseHead.Bestiary

	Fables: {
		Name: The Great Wyvern's Corpse
		Title: Victim of the Gravest Crime
	}
}

WyvernCorpseLegs.DisplayName: The Great Wyvern's Corpse
WyvernCorpseTail.DisplayName: The Great Wyvern's Corpse

NightmareRoseBoss: {
	DisplayName: Nightmare Rose
	BossBarDisplayName: N i g h t m a r e  R o s e
	InternalName: NightmareRose
	DespawnMessage: The amalgamation disbands...
	ExitBarrierDeath: "{0} attempted to flee."
	EternityBarrierDeath: "{0} was eradicated."
	BestiaryEntry1:
		'''
		"Mother Darkness is never too cut-and-dry, and that extends to her motivations and actions.
		Many, many years ago, Mother Darkness took a son under her wing. Nobody knew how old, nobody knew his name.
		To both himself and observers, his destiny was forever postponed, year after year. He had nothing waiting for him in some distant future,
		as all mother darkness needed from him was his warm, bubbly personality to brighten her days and when it served her interests.
		Since word rarely ever escapes the shade world, nobody knew how, when, or even if, certain things developed.
		One thing is known, though. Hekate, the Deity of Witchcraft and Mischief, saw more potential in the boy than his mother did."
		- Transcripts of the late Terníf the Holy.
		'''
	BestiaryEntry2:
		'''
		"The boy had a humanity to him when he wasnt living the sweet life around his mother. He enjoyed observing bugs, designing jewelery, and drawing silt mandalas.
		This, Hekate took the greatest note of during their brief visits to the shade world. This boy had an appreciation for the fleeting, something Hekate often sought out
		in order to find like-minded co-conspirators for their many stunts. On one particular visit to the shade world, Hekate was disguised as a miserly, elderly churl.
		They said to the boy 'You are not loved here. You are merely a tool for her satisfaction. You know this, do you not?' It was on that day that Mother Darkness would no
		longer locate her son in the shade world, as he had left to become an apprentice of Hekate, under the guise of seizing his true potential..."
		- Excerpt from 'Folk Tales of Pherasia: Volume LXXIII', by Uriel XXV.
		'''
	BestiaryEntry3:
		'''
		"Last anyone had heard from Idri, he was ill. Gravely so. Many were confused, like Hekate was, as Idri was a demigod.
		There was no way he would fall victim to any run-of-the-mill illness, so accusations of poison were leveled at Hekate in droves, which led to the destruction
		of their cottage by a mob. While they easily could have rebuilt their cottage, being a god and all, they decided that the people of Pherasia had made their point
		perfectly clear, disappearing to a faraway land to live out their new aspirations of being a gardener."
		- Transcripts of the late Terníf the Holy.
		'''

	Fables: {
		Name: The Nightmare Rose

		Title: {
			Default: Idri's Fate
			Eternity: Idri's Torment
			Masochist: Idri's Husk
		}
	}
}

EimvurNPC: {
	DisplayName: Blood Goddess

	TownNPCMood: {
		Content: I could be worse.
		NoHome: I'd be okay with a nomadic lifestyle if this human body wasnt so sensitive...
		FarFromHome: It seems I'm a long way from home.
		LoveSpace: It is Comfortably Spacious here.
		DislikeCrowded: Walking as a goddess amongst men I would think I'd be treated a little more highly than this compaction.
		HateCrowded: This is deplorable. I ought to kill you at this point.
		LoveBiome: "{BiomeName} Makes me quite happy. Its the closest I can get to a bloody world."
		LikeBiome: "{BiomeName}. Not much to say here."
		DislikeBiome: I'd rather be elsewhere...
		HateBiome: My goodness, {BiomeName}, eugh. Get me out of here right now.
		LoveNPC: I love {NPCName}.
		LikeNPC: I like {NPCName}.
		DislikeNPC: I dislike {NPCName}.
		HateNPC: I hate {NPCName}.
		LikeNPC_Princess: I like {NPCName}. Pink cutie. Heh...
		Princess_LovesNPC: I feel enamored by {NPCName} and her divine prescence. Though, I fear she may want me around more often than I would be comfortable with...
	}
}

